  "ingredients": [
    "3 ounce bacon",
    "1 cup mozzarella cheese (shredded)",
    "2 tablespoon butter",
    "6 large egg",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)",
    "1/2 medium avocado",
    "1 ounce cheddar cheese (shredded)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 375F. Line a baking sheet with foil and bake the bacon for around 15–20 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-breakfast-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51855-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/01Cook-bacon.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, heat up small portions of mozzarella at a time in a clean pan over medium heat, spreading the cheese out thinly. These are going to be our taco shells.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-breakfast-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51855-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/02Melt-mozz.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wait until the cheese is browned on the edges (about 2–3 minutes). Slide a spatula underneath to unstick it from the pan. This should be pretty easy, if using whole-milk mozzarella, as the oil from the cheese will prevent it from sticking.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-breakfast-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51855-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/03Wait-until-browed.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use a pair of tongs to lift the shell up, and drape it over a wooden spoon resting on a pot to form a taco shell shape. Repeat with the remaining mozzarella.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-breakfast-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51855-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/04Drape-over-spoon.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the butter to the pan and cook the eggs, stirring occasionally until cooked through. Season with salt and pepper.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-breakfast-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51855-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/05Scramble-eggs.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Spoon the scrambled eggs into each hardened taco shell.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-breakfast-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51855-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/06Add-eggs.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add some sliced avocado on top.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-breakfast-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51855-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/07Add-avocado.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Next, add the bacon (either chopped or in whole strips).",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-breakfast-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51855-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/08Chop-and-add-bacon.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Finally, sprinkle the shredded cheddar cheese over the breakfast tacos. Enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-breakfast-tacos/#wprm-recipe-51855-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
